            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0784" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4A6/393: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chairman of the
                        American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-13T17:00:00-04:00">July 13, 1931—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Your 44, July 13 [<hi rendition="#italic">12</hi>], 3 p.m. Delegates should
                    remain Geneva pending further instructions. Telegraph full final text to
                    Department <pb facs="0785" n="671" xml:id="pg671"/> and to Berne for forwarding
                    to Wilson, asking Wilson urgently to telegraph comments to you and to
                    Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
